%N A398251 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} H(k,3) / 2^k, where H(k,3) = A007408(k)/A007409(k) is the k-th harmonic number of order 3.
%H A398251 Necdet Batir, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1142/S179304211750097X">On some combinatorial identities and harmonic sums</a>, International Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 13, No. 7 (2017), pp. 1695-1709; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.06401">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:1703.06401 [math.NT], 2017.
%H A398251 Michael I. Shamos, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20220206102634/https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.366.9997&amp;rep=rep1&amp;type=pdf">A catalog of the real numbers</a>, 2011. See p. 124.
%H A398251 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-02462-8">(Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer International Publishing, 2019, section 3.28, p. 159.
%H A398251 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A398251 Equals 7*zeta(3)/4 - log(2)*zeta(2) + log(2)^3/3.
%F A398251 Equals 2 * Li_3(1/2) = 2 * A099217.
%F A398251 Equals Integral_{x=0..1} log(1-x)^2/(1+x) dx (Vălean, 2019).
%F A398251 Equals Integral_{x>=1} log(x)^2/(x*(2*x-1)) dx.
%F A398251 Equals Integral_{x>=0} x^2/(2*exp(x)-1) dx.
%F A398251 Equals Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * (H(k)^2 + H(k,2))/k, where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number, and H(k,2) = A007406(k)/A007407(k) is the k-th harmonic number of order 2 (Batir, 2017, p. 11).
%e A398251 1.074426387216080401881246451189931653340804998680756...
%t A398251 RealDigits[7*Zeta[3]/4 - Log[2]*Zeta[2] + Log[2]^3/3, 10, 120][[1]]
%o A398251 (PARI) 7*zeta(3)/4 - log(2)*zeta(2) + log(2)^3/3
%Y A398251 Cf. A001008, A002805, A007406, A007407, A007408, A007409.
%Y A398251 Cf. A002117, A002162, A013661, A099217.
